## Erlang VM args for ArkAChat
##
## SECURITY: Erlang distribution is DISABLED by default (no -name / -sname).
## Distribution is remote-code-execution by design: anyone who can reach the
## distribution port with the cluster cookie owns the node. For that reason a
## cookie must NEVER be committed to this file.
##
## To enable clustering at deploy time:
##   1. Uncomment the -name line below (or pass it via the release start
##      script).
##   2. Do NOT add -setcookie here. Provision the cookie out-of-band: write a
##      strong random value from your secret manager to ~/.erlang.cookie with
##      mode 0400 before first start. If the file is absent, Erlang generates
##      a random cookie itself; either way it never lives in the repo.
##   3. Keep the loopback binding below and firewall EPMD (tcp/4369) and the
##      distribution port range; prefer TLS distribution for multi-host.
##
## -name arkachat@127.0.0.1

## Defense in depth: if distribution is ever enabled, bind the distribution
## listener to loopback only.
-kernel inet_dist_use_interface {127,0,0,1}
+K true
+A 16
-env ERL_MAX_PORTS 65536
